cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this version of the formalization when using its arbitrary-field
  extension or Lean proof. Cite the original OpenAI construction separately.
type: software
title: 'Matrix multiplication exponent at most 9/4 over arbitrary fields: a Lean formalization'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-07'
authors:
  - family-names: Navot
    given-names: Sela
repository-code: 'https://github.com/selanavot/matrix-multiplication-all-fields'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A Lean formalization extending OpenAI's matrix multiplication exponent bound
  of 9/4 from the complex numbers to every field, including finite fields and
  fields of positive characteristic. OpenAI supplied the original numerical
  bound, complex-field construction, and arithmetic-program specification.
  Sela Navot directed GPT-6 Astra and GPT-6.1 Sol agents in developing and
  formalizing the arbitrary-field extension. This release records exact
  coefficient-rank identities and division-free arithmetic-operation bounds
  with every positive exponent slack. The proof passed Palomar's mechanical
  verification using Lean and the independent kernels recorded in the archived
  report. Palomar's automated review is pending as of 2026-10-07; no human peer
  review or historical-priority claim is made. This is an asymptotic arithmetic
  bound, not a practical implementation or a bit-complexity result. Five
  vendored fixed-point proof modules retain their separate MIT license.
keywords:
  - matrix multiplication
  - arithmetic complexity
  - finite fields
  - tensor rank
  - Lean
  - formal verification
references:
  - type: software
    title: 'An Upper Bound of 9/4 for the Matrix Multiplication Exponent'
    authors:
      - name: OpenAI
